public enum NormalizationForm {
  Composed();
  Decomposed();
}

public enum NormalizationError {
  TooLarge();
}

public fn normalize(form: NormalizationForm, text: &[u32], output: &Box<Slots<u32>>) -> result: Result<unit, NormalizationError> reads(text), writes(output) contract {
  requires text^.len <= 268435456_u64;
} doc "Appends the normalization of text to output, after output's existing contents: Normalization Form C for Composed and Normalization Form D for Decomposed, as Unicode Standard Annex #15 defines them for Unicode 17.0.0, with decompositions, canonical combining classes and composition exclusions from that version's UnicodeData.txt and DerivedNormalizationProps.txt, and Hangul syllables composed and decomposed arithmetically. A value in text that is not a Unicode scalar value is copied unchanged and acts as a starter with no decomposition. The time is linear in the length of text, a long run of combining marks included. TooLarge when output would pass its storage limit; output then holds exactly its prior contents.";
